Ingredients:

4 cups milk
70 gram corn starch
70 gram sugar
1 packet gelitan (optional)


Instructions:

Pour the milk into a large liqid measure, cover, and set aside for a couple hours to bring to room temprature (optional).

Put the dry ingredients in a medium saucepan or fudgepot and whisk together.

Add the milk slowly in between stirring and breaking up clumps until the clumps are gone than add the rest.

Put the saucepan on high heat and constantly stir until it thickens. When it begins to bubble at the edges it's close to being done.

Pour into a tempered glass container that will hold it (if using the one you used to measure the milk, whipe out the milk first) let it set in the fridge for four hours.
